      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough’s original name was “Lock 4,” a nod to the nearby Lock and Dam #4 that once sat on the Monongahela River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Charleroi%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lock and Dam #4 was later moved upstream, leaving the bridge as the only remaining reminder of the original lock on the river’s east bank.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Charleroi%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "North Charleroi sits in Washington County, just north of Charleroi Borough and south of Monessen in Westmoreland County.",
